#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:2
msgid "How to manage versions automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:4
msgid ""
"In this guide, we show you how to define rules to automate creation of new "
"versions on Read the Docs, using your Git repository's version logic. "
"Automating your versioning on Read the Docs means you only have to handle "
"your versioning logic in Git."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:11
msgid ":doc:`/versions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:12
msgid "Learn more about versioning of documentation in general."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:14
msgid ":doc:`/automation-rules`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:15
msgid "Reference for all different rules and actions possible with automation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:18
msgid "Adding a new automation rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:20
msgid "First you need to go to the automation rule creation page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:22
msgid "Go to your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Automation rules`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:23
msgid ""
"Click on :guilabel:`Add automation rule` and you will see the following form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:25
msgid "Screenshot of the \"Add rule\" form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:28
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Add rule` form, fill in the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:30
msgid ""
"Enter a :guilabel:`Description` that you can refer to later. For example, "
"entering \"Create new stable version\" is a good title, as it explains the "
"intention of the rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:34
msgid ""
"Choose one or more :guilabel:`Version types`: *Branch*, *Tag*, or *Pull "
"request*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:37
msgid ""
"Choose a :guilabel:`Version predefined match pattern`, which is the pattern "
"you wish to detect in the version name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:40
msgid ""
":ref:`Any version <automation-rules:Predefined matches>` matches all values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:41
msgid ""
":ref:`SemVer versions <automation-rules:Predefined matches>` matches only "
"values that have the `SemVer`_ format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:42
msgid ""
":ref:`Custom match <automation-rules:Custom matches>` matches your own "
"pattern. If you choose this option, enter a regular expression in `Python "
"regex format`_ in the :guilabel:`Version match pattern` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:46
msgid ""
"Optionally, fill in the webhook match patterns to only match on specific "
"files, pull request labels, or commit messages. See :ref:`automation-"
"rules:Webhook filters`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:49
msgid "Finally, choose the :guilabel:`Action`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:51
msgid ":ref:`Activate version <automation-rules:Version actions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:52
msgid ":ref:`Hide version <automation-rules:Version actions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:53
msgid ":ref:`Make version public <automation-rules:Version actions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:54
msgid ":ref:`Make version private <automation-rules:Version actions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:55
msgid ":ref:`Set version as default <automation-rules:Version actions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:56
msgid ":ref:`Delete version <automation-rules:Version actions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:57
msgid ":ref:`Trigger build for version <automation-rules:Build actions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:60
msgid ""
"Now your rule is ready and you can press :guilabel:`Add rule`. The rule "
"takes effect immediately when a new version is created, but does not apply "
"to old versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:66
msgid "Examples of common usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:67
msgid ""
"See :ref:`the list of examples <automation-rules:Examples>` for rules that "
"are commonly used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:69
msgid "Want to test if your rule works?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:70
msgid ""
"If you are using Git in order to create new versions, create a Git tag or "
"branch that matches the rule and check if your automation action is "
"triggered. After the experiment, you can delete both from Git and Read the "
"Docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:79
msgid "Ordering your rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:81
msgid ""
"The order your rules are listed in your project's :menuselection:`Settings --"
"> Automation rules` matters. Each action will be performed in that order, so "
"earlier rules have a higher priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:85
msgid "You can change the order using the up and down arrow buttons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/automation-rules.rst:89
msgid ""
"New rules are added at the start of the list (i.e. they have the highest "
"priority)."
msgstr ""
